From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 10:14:33 -0400
Subject: sessions: the isolation flag, rebinds that keep sleep and history,
 Clear Independent Session, Focus and the coat in the switcher

Independent session was a token alone: turning it off cleared the token,
so turning it on again made a new, empty jar and left the old one on disk
unreachable. Isolation is now a flag beside the token
(RegistryEntry::isolated); off keeps the token, on again reattaches the
same jar, and a registry written before the flag existed reads a token
as on. Rebinding a tab to another jar restores its serialized entries
and keeps WasDiscarded, so a sleeping tab stays asleep with its history
and the user's name for it; an awake tab reloads. Clear Independent
Session on the Space chip menu wipes an isolated jar (site data and the
HTTP cache) in place. A registry with no PrefService, a Blank Window's,
gets in-memory jars. The sidebar file carries the flag, not the token.

Focus This Space and Hide Other Spaces now reach the switcher: the
active chip alone, no "+", chip drag off, until the flag clears. The
Open in Throwaway row is withdrawn until a throwaway Space is forgotten
when it closes (throwaway T2).

Why: docs/features/sessions.md S2, S7, S9, S13, S18, S19; focus Fc1;
share-coat Sc1; the 2026-09-18 audit (docs/HANDOFF.md, trap 46).
Removable when: patches 0046-0048 fold into upstream or go.
